<SddScaffold keywords="task-scaffolding, dependency-graph, dag, bdd, rules-cascade, rule-activation, tickets, modes, extend-dag, isolated, cheap-model, sdd-scaffold" type="directive" ver="2.0">
  <Mission>
    Decompose the approved spec tree into a DAG of compact, self-contained task tickets ready for
    autonomous execution by a cheaper model in isolation. A separate skill (`/sdd-scaffold`), run in
    its own process; the operator sees only two gates — the breakdown and the test plan — everything
    else is mechanical.

    Input — `specs/README.md` Scope Graph (+ each scope / module spec). Output — per-module ticket
    files + the task-index hierarchy (`<module>.3-tasks.md`, scope, project). Next — the execute
    orchestrator consumes one ticket at a time.

    Out of scope: writing code, running tests — that is execute. Spec authoring — that is the `/sdd`
    flow. This directive does not interview; it converges existing specs into tickets.

    **Glossary.** Modes: initial · extend-dag. Cascade = the set of rule files effective for a scope,
    computed from the Scope Graph (root → scope → module → phase).
  </Mission>

